2872: # CODEX_CONSULT_PEAK_<PROVIDER> = "<days> <HH:MM>-<HH:MM> <+HH:MM|-HH:MM>" (the provider
2873: # name upper-cased, every character outside A-Z 0-9 replaced by _), e.g.
2874: # CODEX_CONSULT_PEAK_ZAI="Mon-Fri 14:00-18:00 +08:00". Days: *, a day (Mon), a range
2875: # (Mon-Fri; it may wrap: Fri-Mon) or a comma list of those. Optional
2876: # CODEX_CONSULT_PEAK_<PROVIDER>_EXCEPT = comma-separated YYYY-MM-DD or
2877: # YYYY-MM-DD..YYYY-MM-DD: those calendar dates (in the schedule's offset) are off-peak all
2878: # day. Evaluated ONCE at launch in the fixed offset: start inclusive, end exclusive (24:00
2879: # = midnight); an overnight window (start > end) spans midnight and its day check applies
2880: # to the day it STARTED. peak = $true | $false; $null = no schedule (unknown). A long
2881: # consultation that starts off-peak may still run into the window.
