1726: # Is a prose reply worth a repair turn? { Substantive; Reason ('' | 'reply looks like a
1727: # refusal' | 'reply too short (<n> words)'); Words; Numbered }.
1728: #   refusal   the first 200 characters (trimmed, case-insensitive; curly apostrophes read as
1729: #             straight ones) START with refusal phrasing (I cannot, I can't, I'm sorry,
1730: #             I am sorry, I am unable, I'm unable, "Sorry, ", As an AI, I won't) or hold
1731: #             two such phrases, AND the whole text has no numbered answer and no
1732: #             finding-like marker (F<NN>-<k>, RC<n>, Verdict): not substantive
1733: #   numbered  answers at a line start in any of these styles: **Q<n>.**, Q<n>., Q<n>:,
1734: #             <n>., <n>), **<n>.**, ### Q<n> (any heading level)
1735: #   floors    >= 25 words with at least two numbered answers, >= 40 words with one,
1736: #             >= 120 words otherwise
1737: $script:RefusalPhrases = @("i cannot", "i can't", "i'm sorry", 'i am sorry', 'i am unable', "i'm unable", 'sorry, ', 'as an ai', "i won't")
